# Ignore rules for `web.Dockerfile`.
#
# That build takes the PARENT of this repository as its context, so the
# repository's own `.dockerignore` — which Docker looks for at the context root
# — never applies. BuildKit reads `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` in preference, so
# these paths are relative to the parent directory and cover both checkouts.
#
# Without this the context is well over a gigabyte of `node_modules` that the
# image reinstalls anyway.

**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/.turbo
**/coverage
**/storybook-static
**/playwright-report
**/test-results
**/blob-report
**/.git
**/.github
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store

# Secrets never belong in an image layer. `.env.example` is kept.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
